    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3 tests, 0 failures) \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only actual test class; the other files under `acceptance/` are the base and helper classes.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**New file \u2014 `service/AddressNormalizer.java`**: a tiny, single-purpose class with one static `normalize` method that trims, collapses internal whitespace, upper-cases, expands `ST\u2192STREET`/`RD\u2192ROAD`/`AVE\u2192AVENUE` (whole-word only, via a lookup map), and throws `IllegalArgumentException` when the address is blank after normalization.\n\n**`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**: added one `@Mapping` line to the existing `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` so the address is normalized during owner creation, via a fully-qualified static expression.\n\n## Why this shape\n\nI deliberately avoided touching `Owner` (a large class \u2014 every edit there pays for the whole class's `WMC_other`), the controller, and `HouseholdMatcher`. Instead I mirrored two patterns already in the codebase:\n\n- **Telephone precedent**: `normalizeTelephone` normalizes in the mapper and throws `IllegalArgumentException` for invalid input, which `ExceptionControllerAdvice` maps to **400** \u2014 so a blank-after-normalization address is rejected the same way.\n- **`householdId` precedent**: it already invokes a `service`-package class via a fully-qualified `expression`, so I did the same rather than adding a method into the mapper's context.\n\nBecause normalization happens at mapping time, the stored/returned `address` is the normalized form, and household duplicate detection (`sameHousehold`) and the shared `householdId` \u2014 both of which read `owner.getAddress()` \u2014 automatically use it, with **no edits** to `HouseholdMatcher`.\n\nStructural impact stays minimal: the only heavy logic lives in a brand-new class whose `WMC_other` is effectively zero, and the sole edit to existing code is a single annotation line on one already-trivial method.\n\n(Note: the observed 400 for the blank case is actually enforced even earlier by the DTO's `.*\\S.*` pattern; the normalizer's own blank-guard is a belt-and-suspenders backstop that keeps the required-field rejection true at the normalization layer too.)",
